taly","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_I_of_Capua","c":2},{"y":1064,"t":"gain","x":"1064: Gaeta passes to the Drengot princes.","cp":"Duchy of Gaeta","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_I_of_Capua","c":3},{"y":1091,"t":"loss","x":"1091: bridging year.","cp":"Duchy of Gaeta","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duchy_of_Gaeta","c":1},{"y":1134,"t":"contest_start","x":"By July 1134: Roger II drives Robert II out of Capua.","m":7,"cp":"kingdom-of-sicily","cpn":"Kingdom of Sicily","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roger_II_of_Sicily","c":2},{"y":1139,"t":"contest_end","x":"July 1139: the war ends at Galluccio and Mignano.","m":7,"cp":"kingdom-of-sicily","cpn":"Kingdom of Sicily","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Principality_of_Capua","c":3},{"y":1139,"t":"loss","x":"July 1139: Capua passes to Roger II.","m":7,"cp":"kingdom-of-sicily","cpn":"Kingdom of Sicily","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Principality_of_Capua","c":2},{"y":1139,"t":"dissolve","x":"July 1139: the principality ends in Roger II's titles.","m":7,"cp":"kingdom-of-sicily","cpn":"Kingdom of Sicily","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Principality_of_Capua","c":2}],"wars":[{"name":"Atenulf's conquest of Benevento","from":899,"to":899,"outcome":"Atenulf I defeated Radelchis II and conquered Benevento in 899; the two principalities were united under one house and declared indivisible (900 on the Pandulf Ironhead page).","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Principality_of_Capua"},{"name":"Henry II's capture of Pandulf IV","from":1022,"to":1022,"outcome":"'In 1022 the prince was taken and a new prince, Pandulf, count of Teano, installed'; Pandulf IV was sent in chains to Henry II and returned only in 1026 after an 18-month siege.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pandulf_IV_of_Capua"},{"name":"Pandulf IV's war with Naples","from":1027,"to":1029,"outcome":"Pandulf deposed Sergius IV of Naples in 1027; Sergius was reinstalled in 1029 by Rainulf's Normans, who received Aversa.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pandulf_IV_of_Capua"},{"name":"Conrad II's expedition to Capua","from":1038,"to":1038,"outcome":"Conrad II besieged and took Capua and gave it to Guaimar IV in May 1038; Pandulf IV fled to Constantinople; Henry III reversed it in 1047.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pandulf_IV_of_Capua"},{"name":"Norman conquest of Capua","from":1057,"to":1058,"outcome":"Richard of Aversa besieged Capua when its prince died in 1057 and took the princely title in 1058; Landulf VIII is recorded as prince until 12 May 1062; Aquino was seized in 1058 and Gaeta incorporated in 1064.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norman_conquest_of_southern_Italy"},{"name":"Roger II's conquest of Capua","from":1134,"to":1139,"outcome":"Robert II was expelled by July 1134 and Roger's son Alfonso installed; Robert returned with a Pisan fleet in 1135 and with the emperor in spring 1137; Roger sacked Capua again, invaded in spring 1138 and after Galluccio (22 July 1139) was proclaimed prince of…","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roger_II_of_Sicily"}],"certainty":[{"from":861,"to":1139,"level":"soft","note":"A small principality in the Campanian plain whose frontier with Naples, Benevento and Salerno is nowhere defined on the pages opened; the Norman extent (the Caserta block) is a reading."}],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Principality_of_Capua","title":"Principality of Capua"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norman_conquest_of_southern_Italy","title":"Norman conquest of southern Italy"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guaimar_IV_of_Salerno","title":"Guaimar IV of Salerno"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pandulf_IV_of_Capua","title":"Pandulf IV of Capua"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pandulf_Ironhead","title":"Pandulf Ironhead"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richard_I_of_Capua","title":"Richard I of Capua"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jordan_I_of_Capua","title":"Jordan I of Capua"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_II_of_Capua","title":"Robert II of Capua"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duchy_of_Gaeta","title":"Duchy of Gaeta"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roger_II_of_Sicily","title":"Roger II of Sicily"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duchy_of_Sorrento","title":"Duchy of Sorrento"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duchy_of_Amalfi","title":"Duchy of Amalfi"}]}